  "slug": "cmb-anisotropic-cosmic-0b9b",
  "summary": "SPT-3G sets A_CB<0.027 and Simons Observatory and LiteBIRD forecasts sharpen CMB tests of photon propagation beyond standard electrodynamics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is using CMB photons as a probe of physics beyond the standard framework, either through their propagation or their interaction history. Two preprints address photon propagation in polarization. An SPT-3G search for anisotropic cosmic birefringence, using two years of data, finds no evidence and sets a new upper limit of A_CB<0.027. A follow-up study on Lorentz-violating electrodynamics updates CPT-odd and CPT-even constraints from CMB polarization and provides forecasts for Simons Observatory and LiteBIRD. A third preprint forecasts how Rayleigh scattering of CMB photons by neutral hydrogen and helium can probe the recombination history and modified recombination scenarios. What is new is the application of CMB polarization data and forecasts to birefringent and Lorentz-violating photon physics, while the Rayleigh scattering study extends the probe to the recombination epoch.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
